course: dictionary
lesson: 13020
title: Fab and friends
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «That's fab, I'll come to your party!» Fab is short for «fabulous», so it means great or wonderful. The speaker is very pleased. The words around it, like «I'll come to your party!», are the clue.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «That's great, I'll come to your party!» still makes sense, so great is a good meaning for fab here.
explain: Fab is informal. You will see it in texts, chats and comics, and people often say it in the UK, Ireland and Australia. Use it with friends, but not in a formal letter or an essay.
fact: «Fab» is short for «fabulous», which means great, wonderful or brilliant.
fact: Fab is informal slang. It is fine in chat and comics, but not in a formal letter or an essay.
fact: Fab is often said in the UK, Ireland and Australia.
fact: A «fab» (as a noun) is a factory that makes computer chips. This is a technical word with a different meaning.
fact: Useful phrases: «fab idea», «you look fab» and «absolutely fab».
exercise: «That's fab, I'll come to your party!» What does fab mean here? | A small animal | Very heavy | *Great and wonderful | Sad and tired
exercise: Ella says, «Your new trainers are fab.» How does Ella feel about the trainers? | Scared of them | Sleepy | Cross and bored | *Pleased and impressed
exercise: «The fab makes computer chips for phones.» What is a fab in this sentence? | A playground | *A factory that makes computer chips | A kind of bird | A type of cake
test: «You look fab in that jacket!» What is the speaker saying? | You look cold | *You look great | You look lost | You look tired
test: In «absolutely fab», which word could replace fab? | heavy | empty | *brilliant | damp
exam: Which sentence uses fab to mean great? | *«We had a fab day at the beach.» | «The fab is cold and grey.» | «The fab sat in the corner of the room.» | «She put the fab on the shelf.»
